#: src/kernel/nix-development.md:1
msgid "Using Nix for Development"
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/nix-development.md:3
msgid ""
"A Nix development shell lets you build and run Asterinas without a Docker "
"container. It provides the same Rust toolchain, QEMU, boot firmware, and "
"host tools as the Docker image, so most build and test instructions in this "
"book work as they are. The differences are listed at the end of this page."
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/nix-development.md:8
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/nix-development.md:10
msgid ""
"You need an x86-64 Linux host with [Nix](https://nixos.org/download/) "
"installed and [flakes enabled](https://wiki.nixos.org/wiki/"
"Flakes#Enabling_flakes_permanently). An ARM64 Linux shell is also provided. "
"It still builds the x86-64 kernel by default, which KVM cannot run on an "
"ARM64 host, so use the `ENABLE_KVM=0` fallback described below."
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/nix-development.md:16
msgid ""
"The Makefile and the build scripts use `/bin/bash`, which does not exist on "
"NixOS by default. On NixOS, enable [envfs](https://github.com/Mic92/envfs) "
"in your system configuration and rebuild the system before entering the "
"shell:"
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/nix-development.md:24
msgid ""
"QEMU uses KVM by default, so `/dev/kvm` must exist and your user must be "
"allowed to open it. If either is not the case, run `make run_kernel "
"ENABLE_KVM=0` to fall back to software emulation, which is much slower."
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/nix-development.md:29
msgid "Enter the development shell"
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/nix-development.md:31
msgid ""
"Clone the repository as described in [Getting Started](../kernel/), then "
"enter the development shell from the root of the checkout:"
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/nix-development.md:38
msgid ""
"The first run downloads the dependencies and builds the packages that no "
"public binary cache provides, such as QEMU and the firmware. This can take a "
"long time."
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/nix-development.md:43
msgid ""
"Inside the shell, the Make targets work as they do in the Docker container. "
"Build and run Asterinas with the same commands as in [Getting Started](../"
"kernel/#getting-started), and see [Advanced Build and Test Instructions]"
"(advanced-instructions.md) for the test targets."
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/nix-development.md:47
msgid "Editors and direnv"
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/nix-development.md:49
msgid ""
"The shell includes `rust-analyzer` from the same nightly as the Rust "
"toolchain. Start your editor from inside the shell so that it inherits the "
"toolchain and the `VDSO_LIBRARY_DIR` variable, which `rust-analyzer` needs "
"in order to check the kernel crate. For example, if VS Code is installed on "
"your host:"
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/nix-development.md:60
msgid ""
"If you use [direnv](https://direnv.net/), the `.envrc` at the repository "
"root activates the shell whenever you enter the checkout. Run `direnv allow` "
"once to approve it."
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/nix-development.md:64
msgid "Differences from the Docker environment"
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/nix-development.md:66
msgid ""
"The Docker image already contains the test suites and benchmarks prebuilt. "
"The shell builds them on demand instead. The first time you run a test "
"target, the initramfs build fetches the selected tests and their runtime "
"dependencies with Nix, which adds time to that first run."
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/nix-development.md:71
msgid ""
"The gVisor syscall tests are built with Bazel inside the Docker image, "
"together with a set of shared libraries that the shell does not provide. Use "
"the Docker environment to run them."
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/nix-development.md:75
msgid ""
"Projects created by `cargo osdk new` and the TDX scheme of the OSDK test "
"suite contain firmware paths specific to the Docker image. They do not work "
"in the shell unless you edit those paths yourself."
msgstr ""

#: src/kernel/nix-development.md:79
msgid ""
"The shell points `OVMF_DIR` at the firmware in the Nix store. If you "
"override it, choose a path without spaces, because the shared QEMU scripts "
"do not quote the value of `OVMF_DIR`."
msgstr ""
